<title>USA: CIT Group sells $100 mln in notes.</title>
<headline>CIT Group sells $100 mln in notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue from CIT Group Holdings Inc was priced on Thursday, according to lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston Corp</p>
<p>CIT Group Holdings is 80 percent owned by Dai-Ichi Kangyo</p>
<p>Bank Ltd and 20 percent owned by Chase Manhattan Corp.</p>
<p>BORROWER CIT GROUP HOLDINGS INC</p>
<p>AMT $100 MLN	 COUPON 6.80 PCT   MATURITY 4/17/2000</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.94   FIRST PAY DATE 10/17/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 6.822 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-PLUS    SPREAD 23 BP	CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
